00:22:41,982 --> 00:22:44,222
To see this tremendous ignorance.

559
00:22:44,242 --> 00:22:45,702
This tremendous destruction.

560
00:22:45,722 --> 00:22:47,582
We are getting at it. We are getting at it.

561
00:22:47,602 --> 00:22:48,802
We are getting at it.

562
00:22:48,822 --> 00:22:49,822
Right.

563
00:22:50,462 --> 00:22:53,962
But then if I don't fully perceive...

564
00:22:53,982 --> 00:22:56,882
if I start to escape the perception of it...

565
00:22:58,522 --> 00:22:59,882
then I'm in it too.

566
00:22:59,882 --> 00:23:01,382
Yes, you are in it too.

567
00:23:01,401 --> 00:23:07,762
But the feeling is still...

568
00:23:08,782 --> 00:23:11,721
that universal sorrow is still something that I can feel.

569
00:23:11,741 --> 00:23:13,161
I mean, is that what you mean to say?

570
00:23:13,181 --> 00:23:14,001
Yes.

571
00:23:14,022 --> 00:23:15,182
Although I am not very

572
00:23:15,182 --> 00:23:16,342
perceptive as to what it means.

573
00:23:16,362 --> 00:23:17,681
No, no, no.

574
00:23:18,822 --> 00:23:21,522
You can feel the sorrow of thought.

575
00:23:21,542 --> 00:23:23,741
The sorrow of thought. But I can sense...

576
00:23:23,762 --> 00:23:26,741
or somehow be aware of the universal sorrow.

577
00:23:26,762 --> 00:23:28,001
Yes, you can. Right.

578
00:23:28,022 --> 00:23:29,582
You say the universal sorrow is there...

579
00:23:29,582 --> 00:23:30,582
whether you feel it.

580
00:23:30,602 --> 00:23:31,901
You can feel it. You can feel it.

581
00:23:31,921 --> 00:23:33,582
Feel it or sense it. Right.

582
00:23:33,602 --> 00:23:34,602
Right.

583
00:23:35,262 --> 00:23:38,362
The sorrow of man living like this.

584
00:23:38,382 --> 00:23:39,822
Is that the essence of it?

585
00:23:39,842 --> 00:23:42,181
I'm just moving into it. Let's move into it.

586
00:23:42,201 --> 00:23:43,181
Is there more to it?

587
00:23:43,201 --> 00:23:44,302
Much more to it.

588
00:23:44,322 --> 00:23:45,392
Oh, well. Then perhaps we

589
00:23:45,392 --> 00:23:46,462
should try to bring that out.

590
00:23:46,482 --> 00:23:47,742
I'm trying to.

591
00:23:48,062 --> 00:23:48,862
There is...

592
00:23:48,882 --> 00:23:49,882
Sorrow, yes.

593
00:23:49,901 --> 00:23:50,901
You see me.

594
00:23:52,641 --> 00:23:54,582
I live the ordinary life.

595
00:23:55,302 --> 00:23:58,342
Image, sorrow, fear, anxiety, all that.

596
00:23:59,582 --> 00:24:02,901
I have the sorrow of self-pity.

597
00:24:02,921 --> 00:24:03,962
Right.

598
00:24:03,982 --> 00:24:04,982
All that.

599
00:24:05,002 --> 00:24:10,901
And you who are enlightened, in quotes...

600
00:24:10,921 --> 00:24:13,191
look at me and say, aren't

601
00:24:13,191 --> 00:24:15,462
you full of sorrow for me?

602
00:24:15,482 --> 00:24:16,762
Which is compassion.

603
00:24:16,782 --> 00:24:19,401
I would say that is a kind of energy...

604
00:24:19,421 --> 00:24:23,201
which is tremendously aroused because of this situation.

605
00:24:23,222 --> 00:24:24,022
Yes. Right?

606
00:24:24,042 --> 00:24:25,042
Yes.

607
00:24:25,062 --> 00:24:27,121
But would you call it

608
00:24:27,121 --> 00:24:29,181
sorrow? Or you call it compassion?

609
00:24:29,182 --> 00:24:32,502
Compassion, which is the outcome of sorrow.

610
00:24:32,522 --> 00:24:34,682
But have you felt sorrow first?

611
00:24:36,102 --> 00:24:37,892
I mean, has the enlightened

612
00:24:37,892 --> 00:24:39,682
person felt sorrow and then compassion?

613
00:24:39,702 --> 00:24:40,702
No.

614
00:24:40,722 --> 00:24:41,722
The other way?

615
00:24:41,742 --> 00:24:43,582
No, no, no. Be careful.

616
00:24:43,602 --> 00:24:45,942
I'll go very carefully.

617
00:24:45,962 --> 00:24:47,862
Which is...

618
00:24:49,582 --> 00:24:53,942
You see, sir, you are saying...

619
00:24:53,962 --> 00:24:57,422
that one must have sorrow first to have compassion.

620
00:24:57,442 --> 00:24:59,162
I'm just exploring.

621
00:24:59,202 --> 00:25:00,722
Yes, we are exploring.

622
00:25:00,742 --> 00:25:03,782
Through sorrow you come to compassion.

623
00:25:03,802 --> 00:25:05,422
That's what you seem to be saying.

624
00:25:05,442 --> 00:25:07,242
Yes, I seem to be saying.

625
00:25:07,262 --> 00:25:09,742
But which implies...

626
00:25:11,102 --> 00:25:13,402
that I must go through all

627
00:25:13,402 --> 00:25:15,702
the horrors of mankind in order.

628
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:16,822
Right.

629
00:25:17,742 --> 00:25:18,502
No.

630
00:25:18,522 --> 00:25:19,942
No? No.

631
00:25:19,962 --> 00:25:21,242
But let's say...

632
00:25:21,262 --> 00:25:22,242
That's the point, sir.

633
00:25:22,262 --> 00:25:25,422
Let's say the enlightened one, the enlightened man...

634
00:25:26,102 --> 00:25:28,942
sees this sorrow, sees this destruction...

635
00:25:28,942 --> 00:25:32,622
and he feels something, he senses something...

636
00:25:32,642 --> 00:25:34,382
which is a tremendous energy.

637
00:25:34,402 --> 00:25:36,382
We call it compassion.

638
00:25:36,402 --> 00:25:37,702
Now, does he...

639
00:25:37,722 --> 00:25:40,682
he understands that the people are in sorrow...

640
00:25:40,702 --> 00:25:41,802
Of course.

641
00:25:41,822 --> 00:25:43,422
But he is not himself in sorrow.

642
00:25:43,442 --> 00:25:45,442
That's right.

643
00:25:46,042 --> 00:25:48,582
But he feels a tremendous energy to do something.

644
00:25:48,602 --> 00:25:51,122
Yes. Tremendous energy of compassion.

645
00:25:51,142 --> 00:25:53,462
Compassion, feeling for them.

646
00:25:53,482 --> 00:25:54,482
Compassion.

647
00:25:54,502 --> 00:25:57,082
Would you then say that he...

648
00:25:57,102 --> 00:25:58,942
that the enlightened man...

649
00:25:58,962 --> 00:26:01,702
perceives or is aware of...

650
00:26:02,842 --> 00:26:03,842
the...

651
00:26:03,862 --> 00:26:04,862
the...

652
00:26:04,882 --> 00:26:07,482
I hate to use the word inefficiency...

653
00:26:07,502 --> 00:26:09,142
but the conflict, the...

654
00:26:09,162 --> 00:26:10,762
the...

655
00:26:10,782 --> 00:26:12,402
he is not aware of sorrow...

656
00:26:12,422 --> 00:26:15,762
he is aware of the awkwardness...

657
00:26:15,782 --> 00:26:19,442
the blundering, the loss of life.

658
00:26:19,462 --> 00:26:20,462
No, sir.

659
00:26:20,482 --> 00:26:22,482
Dr. Shainberg, just listen.

660
00:26:23,402 --> 00:26:24,402
You...

661
00:26:26,022 --> 00:26:27,722
have been through all this.

662
00:26:27,742 --> 00:26:28,742
Suppose you have been through...

663
00:26:28,742 --> 00:26:29,742
all the...

664
00:26:29,762 --> 00:26:30,762
Sorrow.

665
00:26:30,782 --> 00:26:31,782
Sorrow.

666
00:26:32,982 --> 00:26:38,322
Image, thought, the sorrow of thought...

667
00:26:38,342 --> 00:26:39,522
the fears, the anxieties...

668
00:26:39,542 --> 00:26:41,662
and you say, I've understood that.

669
00:26:41,682 --> 00:26:43,422
It's over in me.

670
00:26:43,442 --> 00:26:46,782
But you have left very little.

671
00:26:46,802 --> 00:26:48,622
You have energy.

672
00:26:48,642 --> 00:26:51,562
But you have... it's a very shallow business.

673
00:26:51,582 --> 00:26:58,102
And is life so shallow as all that?

674
00:26:58,122 --> 00:26:58,562
Or...

675
00:26:58,562 --> 00:27:01,322
has it an immense depth?

676
00:27:03,762 --> 00:27:05,222
Depth is the wrong word.

677
00:27:05,242 --> 00:27:07,582
Well, yes, inwardness.

678
00:27:07,602 --> 00:27:09,602
Inwardness.

679
00:27:12,802 --> 00:27:14,802
And to find that out...

680
00:27:17,382 --> 00:27:19,382
don't you have to die...

681
00:27:20,901 --> 00:27:22,901
to everything known?

682
00:27:22,902 --> 00:27:23,902
Yes.

683
00:27:28,902 --> 00:27:29,902
But how does this relate

684
00:27:29,902 --> 00:27:30,902
to sorrow at the same time?

685
00:27:30,922 --> 00:27:31,922
I'm coming...

686
00:27:31,942 --> 00:27:33,942
You might feel...

687
00:27:40,062 --> 00:27:41,062
I'm ignorant.

688
00:27:41,082 --> 00:27:44,082
I have my anxieties, all the rest of it.

689
00:27:47,182 --> 00:27:48,182
You are beyond it.

690
00:27:48,202 --> 00:27:49,702
You are on the other side

691
00:27:49,702 --> 00:27:51,202
of the stream, as it were.

692
00:27:52,902 --> 00:27:54,902
Don't you have compassion?

693
00:27:54,902 --> 00:27:56,902
Don't you have compassion?

694
00:27:56,922 --> 00:27:57,922
Yes.

695
00:27:57,942 --> 00:27:58,942
I do.

696
00:27:58,962 --> 00:27:59,962
I see that.

697
00:27:59,982 --> 00:28:00,962
Not up here.

698
00:28:00,982 --> 00:28:01,982
No, I know.

699
00:28:02,002 --> 00:28:03,002
But I see it and I...

700
00:28:03,022 --> 00:28:04,022
Compassion.

701
00:28:04,042 --> 00:28:05,042
Yes.

702
00:28:06,902 --> 00:28:09,902
Is that the result of the ending of sorrow...

703
00:28:10,902 --> 00:28:12,902
universal sorrow?

704
00:28:12,922 --> 00:28:13,902
What? Universal sorrow?

705
00:28:13,922 --> 00:28:14,902
Universal sorrow.

706
00:28:14,922 --> 00:28:16,902
Wait, let's say the ending of sorrow.

707
00:28:16,922 --> 00:28:18,902
Now, that's not the end of the world.

708
00:28:18,922 --> 00:28:19,902
That's the end of the world.

709
00:28:19,922 --> 00:28:21,002
That's the end of the world.

710
00:28:21,022 --> 00:28:22,222
That's the end of the world.

711
00:28:22,222 --> 00:28:24,222
Now, you are talking about the person...

712
00:28:24,242 --> 00:28:26,222
who was in sorrow to begin with.

713
00:28:26,242 --> 00:28:27,242
Yes.

714
00:28:27,262 --> 00:28:31,262
And in him this universal sorrow ends.

715
00:28:31,282 --> 00:28:32,282
Is that what you are saying?

716
00:28:32,302 --> 00:28:33,262
No, no.

717
00:28:33,282 --> 00:28:34,282
More than that.

718
00:28:34,302 --> 00:28:36,262
More than that. Well, we have to go slowly.

719
00:28:36,282 --> 00:28:38,262
Because if you say the ending of universal sorrow...

720
00:28:38,282 --> 00:28:40,272
the thing that is puzzling

721
00:28:40,272 --> 00:28:42,262
is to say it still exists.

722
00:28:42,282 --> 00:28:46,262
You see, if the universal sorrow ends...

723
00:28:46,282 --> 00:28:48,262
then it's all gone.

724
00:28:48,282 --> 00:28:49,262
Ah, it's still there.

725
00:28:49,282 --> 00:28:50,262
It's still there.

726
00:28:50,282 --> 00:28:52,222
You see, there is a certain puzzle in language.

727
00:28:52,242 --> 00:28:54,282
So, in some sense the universal sorrow ends...

728
00:28:54,302 --> 00:28:56,282
but in another sense it persists.

729
00:28:56,302 --> 00:28:58,282
Yes. Yes, that's right.

730
00:28:58,302 --> 00:29:00,282
But could we say that if you have an insight...

731
00:29:00,302 --> 00:29:03,282
into the essence of sorrow, of universal sorrow...

732
00:29:03,302 --> 00:29:07,282
then in that sense sorrow ends in that insight.

733
00:29:07,302 --> 00:29:08,282
Yes, that's right.

734
00:29:08,302 --> 00:29:11,282
Although it goes on.

735
00:29:11,302 --> 00:29:13,282
I've got a deeper question, though.

736
00:29:13,302 --> 00:29:14,282
The question is...

737
00:29:14,302 --> 00:29:16,282
I don't think you have understood.

738
00:29:16,302 --> 00:29:18,282
I think I understood that one...

739
00:29:18,302 --> 00:29:21,282
but my question comes before...

740
00:29:21,302 --> 00:29:22,222
which is...

741
00:29:22,242 --> 00:29:25,242
is that here is me...

742
00:29:25,262 --> 00:29:28,242
the image-making has died.

743
00:29:28,262 --> 00:29:31,262
That's the waves.

744
00:29:31,282 --> 00:29:36,282
Now, I come into the sorrow.

745
00:29:36,302 --> 00:29:39,282
You've lost the sorrow of thought.

746
00:29:39,302 --> 00:29:41,282
Right.

747
00:29:41,302 --> 00:29:43,262
The sorrow of thought is gone...

748
00:29:43,282 --> 00:29:44,282
but there is a deeper sorrow.

749
00:29:44,302 --> 00:29:46,282
Is there?

750
00:29:46,302 --> 00:29:48,282
Or are you assuming there is deeper sorrow?

751
00:29:48,302 --> 00:29:50,282
I'm trying to understand what you are saying.

752
00:29:50,282 --> 00:29:53,322
No, no.

753
00:29:53,342 --> 00:29:56,322
I'm saying...

754
00:29:58,362 --> 00:30:03,322
is there compassion...

755
00:30:05,302 --> 00:30:09,322
which is not related to thought?

756
00:30:09,342 --> 00:30:13,342
Or is that compassion born of sorrow?

757
00:30:13,362 --> 00:30:15,282
Born of sorrow.

758
00:30:15,302 --> 00:30:16,342
Born in the sense...

759
00:30:16,362 --> 00:30:18,342
when the sorrow ends there is compassion.

760
00:30:18,362 --> 00:30:19,322
Okay.

761
00:30:19,322 --> 00:30:20,282
That makes sense.

762
00:30:20,302 --> 00:30:22,342
That makes it a little clearer.

763
00:30:26,322 --> 00:30:29,322
When the sorrow of thought...

764
00:30:29,342 --> 00:30:31,322
Not personal sorrow.

765
00:30:31,342 --> 00:30:33,282
Not the sorrow of thought.

766
00:30:33,302 --> 00:30:35,322
Not the sorrow of thought, but something deeper.

767
00:30:35,342 --> 00:30:36,322
Something deeper.

768
00:30:36,342 --> 00:30:38,322
When that sorrow ends...

769
00:30:38,342 --> 00:30:42,322
When that sorrow ends...

770
00:30:42,342 --> 00:30:45,322
then there is a birth of compassion.

771
00:30:45,342 --> 00:30:48,322
Of compassion, of energy.

772
00:30:48,362 --> 00:30:49,322
Now...

773
00:30:49,342 --> 00:30:51,322
Is there not...

774
00:30:51,342 --> 00:30:55,382
a deeper sorrow than the sorrow of thought?

775
00:30:55,382 --> 00:31:05,362
Well, there is the...

776
00:31:05,382 --> 00:31:07,362
David was saying...

777
00:31:07,382 --> 00:31:10,421
the sorrow for ignorance is deeper than thought.

778
00:31:10,441 --> 00:31:15,382
The sorrow for the universal...

779
00:31:15,401 --> 00:31:20,362
calamity of mankind trapped in this sorrow.

780
00:31:20,382 --> 00:31:24,382
The sorrow of a continual repetition of wars and history...

781
00:31:24,401 --> 00:31:28,382
and poverty and people mistreating each other...

782
00:31:28,401 --> 00:31:31,362
that's a deeper sorrow.

783
00:31:31,382 --> 00:31:35,362
That's deeper than the sorrow of thought.

784
00:31:35,382 --> 00:31:37,362
And it is.

785
00:31:43,382 --> 00:31:45,401
Can we ask this question?

786
00:31:45,421 --> 00:31:49,401
What is compassion?

787
00:31:49,421 --> 00:31:50,481
Which is love.

788
00:31:50,502 --> 00:31:53,991
We are using that one

789
00:31:53,991 --> 00:31:57,481
word to cover a wide field.

790
00:31:57,502 --> 00:32:04,401
What is compassion?

791
00:32:04,422 --> 00:32:07,462
Can a man...

792
00:32:07,482 --> 00:32:10,462
who is in sorrow, thought, may...

793
00:32:10,482 --> 00:32:11,522
can he have that?

794
00:32:11,542 --> 00:32:12,522
He can't.

795
00:32:12,542 --> 00:32:14,442
Absolutely cannot.

796
00:32:14,462 --> 00:32:15,562
Right?

797
00:32:15,582 --> 00:32:16,562
Right?

798
00:32:16,582 --> 00:32:17,522
Yes.

799
00:32:17,542 --> 00:32:22,522
Now, when does that come into being?

800
00:32:22,542 --> 00:32:26,522
Without that, life has no meaning.

801
00:32:26,542 --> 00:32:33,522
You have left me without that.

802
00:32:33,522 --> 00:32:34,382
So, you...

803
00:32:34,401 --> 00:32:38,441
if all that you have taken away from me...

804
00:32:38,461 --> 00:32:41,441
is superficial sorrow...

805
00:32:41,461 --> 00:32:43,441
thought and image.

806
00:32:43,461 --> 00:32:49,382
And I feel there is something much more.

807
00:32:49,401 --> 00:32:52,441
I mean, just doing that leaves something empty...

808
00:32:52,461 --> 00:32:54,441
or meaningless, right?

809
00:32:54,461 --> 00:33:00,441
Something much greater than this shallow little business.

810
00:33:02,461 --> 00:33:03,421
Is there...

811
00:33:03,442 --> 00:33:07,422
when we have thought producing sorrow, self-pity...

812
00:33:07,442 --> 00:33:10,482
but also the realisation of the sorrow of mankind...

813
00:33:10,502 --> 00:33:13,482
and could you say the energy which is deeper...

814
00:33:13,502 --> 00:33:15,482
is being in some way...

815
00:33:15,502 --> 00:33:16,482
Moved.

816
00:33:16,502 --> 00:33:18,482
You see, well, first of all, in the sorrow...

817
00:33:18,502 --> 00:33:22,422
this energy is caught up in whirlpools or something.

818
00:33:22,442 --> 00:33:24,462
You see, it's much deeper than...

819
00:33:24,482 --> 00:33:25,482
it's deeper than thought...

820
00:33:25,502 --> 00:33:29,482
but there is some sort of very deep disturbance...

821
00:33:29,502 --> 00:33:30,482
of the energy, right?

822
00:33:30,502 --> 00:33:31,502
Yes, quite right, sir.

823
00:33:31,522 --> 00:33:32,522
Which we call deep sorrow.

824
00:33:32,522 --> 00:33:33,522
Deep sorrow.

825
00:33:33,542 --> 00:33:35,522
Deep sorrow.

826
00:33:35,542 --> 00:33:37,522
Ultimately, it must...

827
00:33:37,542 --> 00:33:40,522
its origin is the blockage in thought though, isn't it?

828
00:33:40,542 --> 00:33:43,522
Yes, that is deep sorrow of mankind.

829
00:33:43,542 --> 00:33:45,522
Yes, the deep sorrow of mankind.

830
00:33:45,542 --> 00:33:47,522
For centuries upon centuries...

831
00:33:47,542 --> 00:33:52,522
it's like a vast reservoir of sorrow.

832
00:33:52,542 --> 00:33:57,522
It's sort of moving around in some way that's disorderly...

833
00:33:57,542 --> 00:34:00,522
Yes.

834
00:34:00,542 --> 00:34:02,522
...and preventing clarity...

835
00:34:02,542 --> 00:34:04,542
and so on. I mean perpetuating ignorance.

836
00:34:04,562 --> 00:34:07,442
Ignorance, perpetuating ignorance, right.

837
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:09,442
Because, you see, if it were not for that...

838
00:34:09,462 --> 00:34:11,442
then man's natural capacity to learn...

839
00:34:11,462 --> 00:34:13,482
would solve all these problems. Is that possible?

840
00:34:13,502 --> 00:34:15,482
That's right.

841
00:34:15,502 --> 00:34:17,482
Right, right.

842
00:34:17,502 --> 00:34:21,482
Unless you three give me...

843
00:34:21,502 --> 00:34:26,482
or help me or show me or have an insight...

844
00:34:26,502 --> 00:34:30,522
into something much greater...

845
00:34:30,542 --> 00:34:32,522
I say, yes, this is very nice...

846
00:34:32,542 --> 00:34:35,482
and I go on. You follow?

847
00:34:35,502 --> 00:34:38,482
Yes.

848
00:34:38,502 --> 00:34:39,992
What we are trying to do,

849
00:34:39,992 --> 00:34:41,482
as far as I can see...

850
00:34:41,502 --> 00:34:48,482
is to penetrate into something beyond death.

851
00:34:48,502 --> 00:34:50,522
Beyond death.

852
00:34:50,542 --> 00:34:52,512
Death, we say, is not

853
00:34:52,512 --> 00:34:54,482
only the ending of the organism...

854
00:34:54,502 --> 00:34:57,482
but the ending of all the...

855
00:34:57,502 --> 00:35:01,462
ending of the content of the consciousness...

856
00:35:01,482 --> 00:35:02,502
and the consciousness...

857
00:35:02,522 --> 00:35:04,502
which we know as it is now.

858
00:35:04,522 --> 00:35:07,442
Is it also the ending of sorrow?

859
00:35:07,462 --> 00:35:09,462
Ending of sorrow of that kind...

860
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:11,462
of the superficial kind.

861
00:35:11,482 --> 00:35:13,462
That's clear.

862
00:35:13,482 --> 00:35:15,462
Yes.

863
00:35:15,482 --> 00:35:17,462
And a man who has gone through all that...

864
00:35:17,482 --> 00:35:20,462
he said, that isn't good enough.

865
00:35:20,482 --> 00:35:25,422
You haven't given me the flower, the perfume...

866
00:35:25,442 --> 00:35:28,462
you've just given me the actress of it.

867
00:35:28,482 --> 00:35:32,422
And now, we three are trying to find...

868
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:36,422
that which is beyond the ashes.

869
00:35:36,442 --> 00:35:38,422
Right.

870
00:35:38,442 --> 00:35:40,422
You say there is something...

871
00:35:40,442 --> 00:35:42,422
there is that which is beyond death.

872
00:35:42,442 --> 00:35:43,422
Absolutely.

873
00:35:43,442 --> 00:35:47,422
Would you say that is eternal?

874
00:35:47,442 --> 00:35:49,422
I don't want to use the word...

875
00:35:49,442 --> 00:35:51,422
You won't use the word, but in some sense...

876
00:35:51,442 --> 00:35:52,422
beyond time.

877
00:35:52,442 --> 00:35:53,422
Beyond time.

878
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:55,422
Therefore, eternal is not the best word for it.

879
00:35:55,442 --> 00:35:58,402
Therefore, there is something

880
00:35:58,402 --> 00:36:01,362
beyond this superficial death...

881
00:36:01,382 --> 00:36:02,422
as eternal.

882
00:36:02,442 --> 00:36:06,422
A movement that has no beginning and no ending.

883
00:36:06,442 --> 00:36:07,422
But it is a movement.

884
00:36:07,442 --> 00:36:09,422
It's a movement.

885
00:36:09,442 --> 00:36:11,422
Movement not in time.

886
00:36:11,442 --> 00:36:13,422
What is the difference between a movement in time...

887
00:36:13,442 --> 00:36:16,422
and a movement out of time?

888
00:36:22,442 --> 00:36:26,422
Sir, that which is constantly renewing...

889
00:36:26,442 --> 00:36:28,422
constantly...

890
00:36:28,442 --> 00:36:29,422
new is in the word...

891
00:36:29,442 --> 00:36:32,422
constantly fresh...

892
00:36:32,442 --> 00:36:33,422
flowering...

893
00:36:33,442 --> 00:36:35,422
endlessly flowering...

894
00:36:35,442 --> 00:36:38,422
that is timeless.

895
00:36:38,442 --> 00:36:40,422
This whole flowering implies time.

896
00:36:40,442 --> 00:36:43,422
Yes, well, I think we can see the point.

897
00:36:43,442 --> 00:36:44,422
I think we get that.

898
00:36:44,442 --> 00:36:47,422
The feel of renewal and creation...

899
00:36:47,442 --> 00:36:51,422
and coming and going without transition...

900
00:36:51,442 --> 00:36:54,422
without duration, without linearity...

901
00:36:54,442 --> 00:36:55,422
that has...

902
00:36:55,442 --> 00:36:58,432
You see, let me come back

903
00:36:58,432 --> 00:37:01,422
to it in a different way.

904
00:37:01,442 --> 00:37:05,422
Being a normally fairly intelligent man...

905
00:37:05,442 --> 00:37:07,422
read various books...

906
00:37:07,442 --> 00:37:10,422
tried various meditations...

907
00:37:10,442 --> 00:37:14,422
Zen and this and that and the other thing...

908
00:37:14,442 --> 00:37:19,422
at one glance I have an insight into all that.

909
00:37:19,442 --> 00:37:21,422
At one glance. It's finished.

910
00:37:21,442 --> 00:37:25,421
I won't touch it.

911
00:37:25,442 --> 00:37:29,421
And it may be...

912
00:37:29,421 --> 00:37:33,421
the ending...

913
00:37:33,441 --> 00:37:37,421
of this image-maker and all that...

914
00:37:37,441 --> 00:37:41,421
there a meditation must take place...

915
00:37:41,441 --> 00:37:45,421
to delve...

916
00:37:45,441 --> 00:37:47,421
to have an insight...

917
00:37:47,441 --> 00:37:53,421
into something which mind has never touched before.

918
00:37:53,441 --> 00:37:54,421
Right.

919
00:37:54,441 --> 00:37:56,421
But I mean, even if you do touch it...

920
00:37:56,441 --> 00:37:58,421
then when you...

921
00:37:58,421 --> 00:38:02,421
That doesn't mean the next time it will be known.

922
00:38:02,441 --> 00:38:04,421
It can never be known.

923
00:38:04,441 --> 00:38:05,431
It can never be known.

924
00:38:05,431 --> 00:38:06,421
It's always new in some sense.

925
00:38:06,441 --> 00:38:08,421
Yes, it's always new.

926
00:38:08,441 --> 00:38:14,422
It is not a memory stored up and altered, changed...

927
00:38:14,442 --> 00:38:16,422
and call it new.

928
00:38:16,442 --> 00:38:21,422
It has never been old.

929
00:38:21,442 --> 00:38:23,422
I don't know if I can put it that way.

930
00:38:23,442 --> 00:38:26,422
Yes, I think I understand that.

931
00:38:26,442 --> 00:38:27,442
It's old.

932
00:38:27,442 --> 00:38:28,942
Could you say it like a

933
00:38:28,942 --> 00:38:30,442
mind that has never known sorrow?

934
00:38:30,462 --> 00:38:32,442
Yes.

935
00:38:32,462 --> 00:38:34,442
It might seem puzzling at first...

936
00:38:34,462 --> 00:38:37,442
but you move out of this state...

937
00:38:37,462 --> 00:38:38,442
which has known sorrow...

938
00:38:38,462 --> 00:38:40,442
into a state which has not known sorrow.

939
00:38:40,462 --> 00:38:41,442
Yes, that's right.

940
00:38:41,462 --> 00:38:43,442
In other words, there is no you.

941
00:38:43,462 --> 00:38:44,442
That's right.

942
00:38:44,462 --> 00:38:45,442
Can we say it this way too?

943
00:38:45,462 --> 00:38:48,442
Could we say that it's an action...

944
00:38:48,462 --> 00:38:50,442
which is moving...

945
00:38:50,462 --> 00:38:53,442
where there is no you?

946
00:38:53,462 --> 00:38:56,442
You see, when you use the word action...

947
00:38:56,442 --> 00:39:00,442
action means not in the future or in the past...

948
00:39:00,462 --> 00:39:03,442
action is the doing.

949
00:39:03,462 --> 00:39:06,442
Yes.

950
00:39:06,462 --> 00:39:10,442
Most of our actions are the result of the cause...

951
00:39:10,462 --> 00:39:13,442
or the past, or according to your future.

952
00:39:13,462 --> 00:39:15,442
Right. This is not that.

953
00:39:15,462 --> 00:39:18,442
That's not action, that's just conformity.

954
00:39:18,462 --> 00:39:21,442
No, I'm talking about a different kind of action.

955
00:39:21,462 --> 00:39:26,342
No, I wouldn't... action implies...

956
00:39:26,362 --> 00:39:26,442
...a certain kind of action.

957
00:39:26,442 --> 00:39:28,442
Yes.

958
00:39:28,462 --> 00:39:32,442
You see, there are several things involved.

959
00:39:32,462 --> 00:39:34,442
To penetrate into this...

960
00:39:34,462 --> 00:39:38,442
the mind must be completely silent.

961
00:39:38,462 --> 00:39:39,442
Right?

962
00:39:39,462 --> 00:39:42,442
Otherwise you are projecting something into it.

963
00:39:42,462 --> 00:39:47,442
Right. It is not projecting into anything.

964
00:39:47,462 --> 00:39:50,442
Absolute silence.

965
00:39:50,462 --> 00:39:56,342
And that silence is not the product of control.

966
00:39:56,342 --> 00:40:01,342
It is wished for, premeditated, predetermined.

967
00:40:01,342 --> 00:40:02,342
Right.

968
00:40:02,362 --> 00:40:06,342
Therefore that silence is not brought about through will.

969
00:40:06,362 --> 00:40:08,342
Right. Right?

970
00:40:08,362 --> 00:40:09,342
Right.

971
00:40:09,362 --> 00:40:14,342
Now, in that silence...

972
00:40:14,362 --> 00:40:17,342
there is...

973
00:40:17,362 --> 00:40:23,342
there is this sense of...

974
00:40:23,362 --> 00:40:26,242
something beyond all time...

975
00:40:26,242 --> 00:40:28,242
death, all thoughts, you follow?

976
00:40:28,262 --> 00:40:30,242
Something...

977
00:40:30,262 --> 00:40:32,242
Yes.

978
00:40:32,262 --> 00:40:38,242
Nothing.

979
00:40:38,262 --> 00:40:40,242
Not a thing. You understand?

980
00:40:40,262 --> 00:40:42,242
Nothing.

981
00:40:42,262 --> 00:40:47,242
And therefore empty, and therefore tremendous energy.

982
00:40:47,262 --> 00:40:49,242
And moving.

983
00:40:49,262 --> 00:40:52,242
Energy. Leave it, leave it.

984
00:40:52,262 --> 00:40:54,242
Is this also the source of compassion?

985
00:40:54,242 --> 00:40:57,242
That is what I... That is it.

986
00:40:57,262 --> 00:40:59,242
What do you mean by source?

987
00:40:59,262 --> 00:41:00,242
Well, that this...

988
00:41:00,262 --> 00:41:02,242
in this energy is compassion, is that...

989
00:41:02,262 --> 00:41:03,242
Yes, that is right.

990
00:41:03,262 --> 00:41:05,242
And in this energy...

991
00:41:05,262 --> 00:41:06,242
This energy is...

992
00:41:06,262 --> 00:41:08,242
...is compassion. That is different.

993
00:41:08,262 --> 00:41:09,242
Of course.

994
00:41:09,262 --> 00:41:12,242
This energy is compassion.

995
00:41:12,262 --> 00:41:15,242
See, that is different than saying the source.

996
00:41:15,262 --> 00:41:20,242
You see, and beyond that there is something more.

997
00:41:20,262 --> 00:41:21,242
Yes. Beyond that.

998
00:41:21,262 --> 00:41:22,302
Of course.

999
00:41:22,322 --> 00:41:24,242
Beyond that. Well, why do you say of course?

1000
00:41:24,262 --> 00:41:26,242
I don't know.

1001
00:41:26,262 --> 00:41:28,242
I don't know.

1002
00:41:28,262 --> 00:41:31,242
What could it be that is more?

1003
00:41:38,262 --> 00:41:43,242
Sir, let's put it a little differently.

1004
00:41:43,262 --> 00:41:47,242
Everything thought has created is not sacred.

1005
00:41:47,262 --> 00:41:49,242
It is not holy.

1006
00:41:49,262 --> 00:41:51,242
Yes, well, because it is fragmented.

1007
00:41:51,262 --> 00:41:52,262
It is fragmented. We know it.

1008
00:41:52,282 --> 00:41:54,242
I am putting up an image...

1009
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:57,242
of worshipping. It is a creation of thought.

1010
00:41:57,262 --> 00:41:59,242
It is made by the hand or by the mind.

1011
00:41:59,262 --> 00:42:01,242
It is still an image.

1012
00:42:01,262 --> 00:42:05,242
So in that there is nothing sacred.

1013
00:42:05,262 --> 00:42:07,242
Because as you pointed out, it is...

1014
00:42:07,262 --> 00:42:10,242
thought is fragmented, limited, finite.

1015
00:42:10,262 --> 00:42:12,242
It is a product of memory and so on.

1016
00:42:12,262 --> 00:42:13,242
So there is nothing sacred.

1017
00:42:13,262 --> 00:42:16,242
It is the sacred therefore that which is without limit.

1018
00:42:16,262 --> 00:42:17,242
That is it.

1019
00:42:17,262 --> 00:42:18,242
I mean...

1020
00:42:18,262 --> 00:42:21,242
There is something beyond compassion...

1021
00:42:21,262 --> 00:42:22,242
Beyond compassion.

1022
00:42:22,262 --> 00:42:23,242
...which is sacred.

1023
00:42:23,242 --> 00:42:24,242
Yes.

1024
00:42:24,262 --> 00:42:26,242
Or is it beyond movement?

1025
00:42:26,262 --> 00:42:28,242
Sacred.

1026
00:42:28,262 --> 00:42:29,242
Sacred.

1027
00:42:29,262 --> 00:42:31,242
You can't say movement or non-movement.

1028
00:42:31,262 --> 00:42:33,242
You can't say anything.

1029
00:42:33,262 --> 00:42:37,242
A living thing...

1030
00:42:37,262 --> 00:42:40,242
you can only examine a dead thing.

1031
00:42:40,262 --> 00:42:43,242
A living thing you can't examine.

1032
00:42:43,262 --> 00:42:45,252
What we are trying to do

1033
00:42:45,252 --> 00:42:47,242
is to examine that living thing...

1034
00:42:47,262 --> 00:42:52,242
which we call sacred, which is beyond compassion.

1035
00:42:52,242 --> 00:42:57,242
What is our relation to the sacred then?

1036
00:42:57,262 --> 00:43:03,242
To the man who is ignorant, there is no relationship.

1037
00:43:03,262 --> 00:43:04,242
Right?

1038
00:43:04,262 --> 00:43:06,242
Which is true.

1039
00:43:06,262 --> 00:43:12,242
To the man who has removed the image, all that...

1040
00:43:12,262 --> 00:43:16,242
who is free of the image and the image-maker...

1041
00:43:16,262 --> 00:43:21,242
is still... it has no meaning yet.

1042
00:43:22,242 --> 00:43:24,242
Right?

1043
00:43:24,262 --> 00:43:28,242
It has meaning only when he goes beyond everything...

1044
00:43:28,262 --> 00:43:32,242
beyond... he dies to everything.

1045
00:43:35,242 --> 00:43:38,242
Dying means in the sense...

1046
00:43:38,262 --> 00:43:43,242
never for a single more second accumulating anything...

1047
00:43:43,262 --> 00:43:46,242
psychologically.

1048
00:43:50,242 --> 00:43:51,242
But would you say...

1049
00:43:51,262 --> 00:43:53,242
would you say that there is any...

1050
00:43:53,262 --> 00:43:54,752
you asked the question, what

1051
00:43:54,752 --> 00:43:56,242
is the relationship to the sacred?

1052
00:43:56,262 --> 00:43:58,752
Is there ever a relationship to

1053
00:43:58,752 --> 00:44:01,242
the sacred or is the sacred...

1054
00:44:01,262 --> 00:44:03,242
No, no, no, he is asking something.

1055
00:44:03,262 --> 00:44:08,242
He is asking what is the relationship between...

1056
00:44:08,262 --> 00:44:13,242
that which is sacred, holy, and to reality.

1057
00:44:13,262 --> 00:44:16,242
Yes, well, that's implicit anyway.

1058
00:44:16,262 --> 00:44:17,242
I mean, that's implied.

1059
00:44:17,262 --> 00:44:19,242
Of course.

1060
00:44:19,262 --> 00:44:21,242
That...

1061
00:44:21,262 --> 00:44:24,242
We've talked about it some time over, this question.

1062
00:44:24,262 --> 00:44:28,242
Which is, reality which is the product of thought...

1063
00:44:28,262 --> 00:44:30,242
has no relationship to that.

1064
00:44:30,262 --> 00:44:35,242
Because thought is an empty little affair.

1065
00:44:35,262 --> 00:44:38,242
That may have a relationship with this.

1066
00:44:38,262 --> 00:44:40,242
In some way, yes.

1067
00:44:40,262 --> 00:44:43,242
Right.

1068
00:44:44,262 --> 00:44:48,242
And the relationship comes through insight...

1069
00:44:48,242 --> 00:44:52,242
insight, intelligence, and compassion.

1070
00:44:54,262 --> 00:44:58,242
How does the... how... how...

1071
00:44:58,262 --> 00:45:01,242
what is that relationship?

1072
00:45:01,262 --> 00:45:05,242
I mean, what is intelligence, I suppose, we are asking?

1073
00:45:05,262 --> 00:45:09,242
Intelligence? What is intelligence?

1074
00:45:10,262 --> 00:45:13,242
I mean, how does intelligence act?

1075
00:45:13,262 --> 00:45:16,242
Wait, wait.

1076
00:45:16,242 --> 00:45:20,242
You have had an insight into the image.

1077
00:45:20,262 --> 00:45:24,242
You have had an insight into the movement of thought.

1078
00:45:24,262 --> 00:45:27,242
Movement of thought which is self-pity, creates sorrow...

1079
00:45:27,262 --> 00:45:28,242
and all that.

1080
00:45:28,262 --> 00:45:31,242
You have had a real insight into it.

1081
00:45:31,262 --> 00:45:33,242
Haven't you?

1082
00:45:33,262 --> 00:45:36,242
It's not a verbal agreement or disagreement...

1083
00:45:36,262 --> 00:45:39,242
or logical conclusion.

1084
00:45:39,262 --> 00:45:43,242
You have had a real insight into that business...

1085
00:45:43,262 --> 00:45:46,242
into the waves of the river.

1086
00:45:46,262 --> 00:45:50,242
Now, have you an insight also...

1087
00:45:50,262 --> 00:45:53,242
isn't that insight intelligence?

1088
00:45:53,262 --> 00:45:55,242
Right.

1089
00:45:55,262 --> 00:45:58,242
Which is not the intelligence of a clever man...

1090
00:45:58,262 --> 00:46:01,242
we are not talking of that.

1091
00:46:01,262 --> 00:46:02,242
So there is that intelligence.

1092
00:46:02,262 --> 00:46:04,242
You have already got that intelligence.

1093
00:46:04,262 --> 00:46:06,242
That's right.

1094
00:46:06,262 --> 00:46:10,242
Now, move with that intelligence...

1095
00:46:10,262 --> 00:46:12,242
which is not yours or mine.

1096
00:46:12,262 --> 00:46:13,242
Intelligence.

1097
00:46:13,262 --> 00:46:16,242
Not Miss Dr. Shenberg or Case...

1098
00:46:16,262 --> 00:46:17,242
or somebody's.

1099
00:46:17,262 --> 00:46:22,242
It is universal intelligence.

1100
00:46:22,262 --> 00:46:26,242
Global or cosmic intelligence.

1101
00:46:26,262 --> 00:46:28,242
That insight.

1102
00:46:28,262 --> 00:46:30,242
Now, move further into it.

1103
00:46:30,262 --> 00:46:33,242
Move with it.

1104
00:46:33,262 --> 00:46:37,242
Have an insight into sorrow...

1105
00:46:37,262 --> 00:46:40,242
which is not the sorrow of thought...

1106
00:46:40,262 --> 00:46:43,242
the enormous sorrow of mankind...

1107
00:46:43,262 --> 00:46:46,242
of ignorance. You follow?

1108
00:46:46,262 --> 00:46:48,242
Yes.

1109
00:46:48,262 --> 00:46:56,242
And then, out of that, insight, compassion.

1110
00:46:56,262 --> 00:47:00,242
Now, insight into compassion.

1111
00:47:07,262 --> 00:47:12,242
Is compassion the end of all life?

1112
00:47:12,262 --> 00:47:15,242
End of all death?

1113
00:47:15,262 --> 00:47:17,242
It seems so, because you have...

1114
00:47:17,262 --> 00:47:19,242
you follow? You have thrown away...

1115
00:47:19,262 --> 00:47:22,242
mind has thrown away all the burdens...

1116
00:47:22,262 --> 00:47:25,242
which man has imposed upon itself.

1117
00:47:25,262 --> 00:47:26,242
Right?

